-- lib-test.once: a LIBRARY (no `main`).
--
-- D008 + "concrete = interface" (the anchor model): a program is anchored by
-- `main : Eff Unit Unit`, which monomorphizes everything composing up to it. A
-- library has no `main`, so its CONCRETE-typed top-level functions ARE the
-- anchors — each signature is a contract that instantiates the polymorphic
-- builtins it uses. Polymorphism is inferred and internal; a library's
-- interface is its concrete signatures.
--
-- (Was `swap : A * B -> B * A` — a polymorphic *signature*, which is ill-formed:
-- signatures are concrete contracts, polymorphism is inferred, never written.)
--
-- Compiled to x86_64 assembly (no entry point); the C library backend
-- (`--lib`) is not yet implemented.

swapII : Int * Int -> Int * Int
swapII = pair snd fst
